<div class="space-y-10">
  <section>
    <h3>Headings provide structure</h3>
    <p>Navigate through these headings with your screen reader's heading controls. Their text describes the content that follows, and their levels form a logical outline.</p>
    <div class="border-2 border-lt-code-border p-4 dark:border-dk-code-border">
      <h4 class="mt-0">Account settings</h4>
      <p>Update your account details and preferences.</p>
      <h5>Notification preferences</h5>
      <p>Choose which notifications you want to receive.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h3>Compare generic and descriptive links</h3>
    <p>Open your screen reader's links list or navigate through these links. The first group repeats generic text; the second identifies each destination.</p>
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="border-2 border-dashed border-lt-code-border p-4 dark:border-dk-code-border">
        <h4 class="mt-0">Problematic link text</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#" data-demonstration-link>Read more</a> about testing headings.</li>
          <li><a href="#" data-demonstration-link>Read more</a> about testing forms.</li>
          <li><a href="#" data-demonstration-link>Click here</a> for screen-reader guidance.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="border-2 border-lt-code-border p-4 dark:border-dk-code-border">
        <h4 class="mt-0">Descriptive link text</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#" data-demonstration-link>Learn how to test headings</a>.</li>
          <li><a href="#" data-demonstration-link>Learn how to test forms</a>.</li>
          <li><a href="#" data-demonstration-link>Read the screen-reader guidance</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-demonstration-link]').forEach((link) => {
    link.addEventListener('click', (event) => event.preventDefault());
  });
</script>
